  "source": "JoyPro curated on the maker's photo (2026-10-12), Virpil's \"VPC SharKa-50 Control Panel\" button-map sheet (flat): one drawing of the panel seen from the front-left and above, the four levers along the back, keypads, push buttons, toggles, a 5-position selector and two knobs on the deck; markers sit on the drawn controls, not on the number labels",
  "mappingSource": "the sheet itself (Virpil support \"VPC SharKa-50 Control Panel\", https://support.virpil.com/en/support/solutions/articles/47001250817-vpc-sharka-50-control-panel, attachment 47246732690). The sheet draws one leader line per box group and chains the dots of a group (e.g. one line through all keys of a keypad), so the number of each control inside a group comes from the box arrangement, which mirrors the physical arrangement",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "note": "traced lines: rY -> rightmost lever (chain through all four levers: X, Y, rX, rY left to right); 2 -> back-right key of the 2x2 keypad (1 2 / 6 7); 3 -> START button (chain START, APU, STOP = 3, 4, 5); 17 -> chain HMS, TC, LAS toggles (14/15, 16/17, 18/19 left to right); 9 -> LH ENG/RH ENG toggle (9 / OFF / 8); OFF of 10/11 -> START/CRANK toggle; 13 -> MASTER ARM toggle (12/13); 21 -> chain through the six-key keypad (back row 20 21 22 23, front row 27 under 21, 28 under 22); 24 -> left knob (BRT; 24 push, 25/26 turn), its dot chained to the right knob (29-31, connected boxes 24-29); 32 -> 5-position selector (32-36); 37 -> MAN/AUTO toggle (37/38); 39 -> LNG/SHORT toggle (39-41); 42 -> HE/API toggle (42/43); 44 -> LOW/HIGH toggle (44/45). the catalog note says the printed labels could not be matched to numbers and gives generic numbers 1-45; the sheet's numbers equal the catalog's JOY_BTN numbers, so these markers make the generic parts usable. Which lever position/selector position is which number inside a toggle group is not drawn; all positions of one control sit on that control.",
